ather than delivering genuine public protection. That objection correctly identifies the risk of regulatory capture, yet it misdiagnoses the remedy by demanding deregulation instead of strict structural accountability. Realizing this risk requires pairing mandatory evaluations with open-source auditing access for independent academic researchers funded by federal oversight grants. The National Science Foundation can administer this neutral evaluation infrastructure to prevent dominant labs from writing their own examination criteria. Without this binding enforcement mechanism backed by named officer liability, society trades fragile corporate self-regulation for unmitigated civilizational collapse.",
